  "boundaries": [
    "Native QDateTimeEdit/QDateEdit/QTimeEdit retain value, range, parsing, section selection, keyboard stepping, native calendar popup and the same QLineEdit.",
    "Calendar Hidden means native stepper, not NoButtons. Native token QSS yields style ownership only for captured date/time instances, preserving the 42px native popup hit region.",
    "DateTime's CST is inert source annotation, not a Qt::TimeSpec mapping or verified timezone policy. It is omitted when Show time is false.",
